    "done_when": "Unit tests of the copied state machine against a stubbed, version-sorted tag list cover every transition imas-codex documents, the v0.0.0 baseline read by both the latest-tag and latest-stable queries, the bare automatic call from stable starting a patch RC, and the push skipped when the tree digest is unchanged. v0.1.0 is tagged in place on the 2026.10.07 artifact and resolves to the same manifest digest. imas-ambix maps release jt-60sa --bump minor publishes v0.2.0-rc1, oras manifest fetch shows its io.imas-ambix machine, git-commit and tree-digest annotations, a second plain call with nothing changed pushes nothing and says so, no --final is run, and git tag -l lists no new tag. imas-ambix maps pull jt-60sa --version v0.2.0-rc1 --dest into a new directory under the run scratch directory reproduces the released tree digest, a pull with no version fetches v0.1.0, and maps status jt-60sa reports RC state, latest stable v0.1.0, latest RC v0.2.0-rc1 and the local tree matching the RC. install/imasdb.sh pulls through maps pull --dest. AGENTS.md tells a coordinator to call release at each landing that changed a bundle, and to declare any write into a machine directory under maps/ (maps/jt-60sa/ today) as an absolute main-checkout path, because a relative maps/ write path leaves the real tree read-only under the write fence. Negative control: against the stubbed registry, a release with the digest check removed pushes a duplicate, which the skip test catches. uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests packages exits 0.",
